+
+# Request
+
+Customers can rent by the hour. `addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice` (euro cents for one hour).
+A rental shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour costs `hourlyPrice × hours`. An item without
+an hourly price cannot be rented by the hour.
+
+# Approach
+
+- `Equipment.hourlyPrice?` is validated like `dailyPrice` (non-negative integer cents) when given.
+- `parsePeriod` accepts a period under 24h whose start and end fall on the hour as an hourly period;
+  longer periods still need midnight UTC bounds. No long-rental discount applies to hours.
+- `quote`/`book` throw for an hourly period on an item without `hourlyPrice`; overlap checks and
+  availability work on instants, so they cover hourly periods unchanged.
+- Tests cover pricing, booking parity, items lacking an hourly price, off-the-hour and 24h+ periods, overlaps.
